[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (F1) at (2.2,1.8);
\coordinate (F2) at (2.2,0);
\coordinate (F3) at (2.2,-1.8);
\draw (O)--(F1) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$1$};
\draw (O)--(F2) node[midway,fill=white,inner sep=1pt,font=\small] {$2$};
\draw (O)--(F3) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$3$};
\draw (F1)--(4.8,2.4);
\draw (F1)--(4.8,1.2);
\draw (F2)--(4.8,0.6);
\draw (F2)--(4.8,-0.6);
\draw (F3)--(4.8,-1.2);
\draw (F3)--(4.8,-2.4);
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,3.2) {Spinner};
\node[font=\small] at (4.8,3.2) {Coin};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A spinner with three equal sectors labelled $1$, $2$ and $3$ is spun, then a coin is tossed.
The spinner stage is already shown and the coin branches are still unlabelled.
Which outcomes belong at the ends of the two branches leaving the $2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (F1) at (2.2,1.5);
\coordinate (F2) at (2.2,-1.5);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,1.5);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,0.6);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-0.6);
\coordinate (E5) at (4.8,-1.5);
\coordinate (E6) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O)--(F1) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$R$};
\draw (O)--(F2) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$B$};
\draw (F1)--(E1) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$1$};
\draw (F1)--(E2) node[midway,fill=white,inner sep=1pt,font=\small] {$2$};
\draw (F1)--(E3) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$3$};
\draw (F2)--(E4) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$1$};
\draw (F2)--(E5) node[midway,fill=white,inner sep=1pt,font=\small] {$2$};
\draw (F2)--(E6) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$3$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E1) {$(R,1)$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E2) {$(R,2)$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E3) {$(R,3)$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E4) {$(B,1)$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E5) {$(B,2)$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E6) {$(B,3)$};
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,3.2) {Spinner $A$};
\node[font=\small] at (4.8,3.2) {Spinner $B$};
\node[font=\small] at (6.3,3.2) {Outcome};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The tree diagram records spinning Spinner $A$ (sectors $R$ and $B$) and then Spinner $B$ (sectors $1$, $2$ and $3$).
How many of the outcomes contain the number $2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (F1) at (2.2,1.5);
\coordinate (F2) at (2.2,-1.5);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.6);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.6);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O)--(F1) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$1$};
\draw (O)--(F2) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$2$};
\draw (F1)--(E1) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$1$};
\draw (F1)--(E2) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$2$};
\draw (F2)--(E3) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$1$};
\draw (F2)--(E4) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$2$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E1) {$(1,1)$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E2) {$(1,2)$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E3) {$(2,1)$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (E4) {$(2,2)$};
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,3.2) {Spin $1$};
\node[font=\small] at (4.8,3.2) {Spin $2$};
\node[font=\small] at (6.1,3.2) {Outcome};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The tree diagram shows the outcomes when a spinner with two equal sectors labelled $1$ and $2$ is spun twice.
The spinner is now spun a third time.
How many outcomes does the three-spin experiment have?
